From d7acab90a8078f8edde5bd4fd95d2593f41808a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:25:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(usage): account-usage refresh claims can no longer wedge
 a slot for the process lifetime [daveey]

Long-lived Desktop backends rendered every pooled account 'unknown': a refresh claim
that leaked (thread start raising under load, a worker dying mid-batch, or a worker
releasing a key re-derived under a different home) blocked that slot forever.

- release (and un-throttle) claims when the refresh thread fails to start
- the per-account worker releases the exact claimed keys, every one, even if a fetch
  escapes; one failing slot no longer starves its siblings
- inflight claims carry a token + clock and expire after INFLIGHT_EXPIRE_S (4x the 15 s
  fetch bound); a stale worker cannot release a newer claim
- read-only diagnostics.account_usage_cache RPC + account_usage_cache_diagnostics()
  (inflight count/ages, last-try and snapshot ages for the scoped home); expiry and
  start failures log a warning
